    "description": "Mid-century corner apartment building located in the heart of the Sunset District. Situated at the intersection of Kirkham and Judah Streets, this spacious apartment building was constructed in 1972 and spans 6,155 square feet. It is comprised of 5 generous two-bedroom, two-bathroom units, each featuring separate dining and living rooms, as well as 1 en-suite bathroom. The property includes garage parking for five cars. There is onsite, coin-operated laundry and each unit is individually metered for gas and electricity keeping operating costs low. Fully stabilized and leased with strong rental income, this property presents an outstanding investment opportunity. Just blocks away, Irving Street's vibrant commercial hub offers a wide variety of restaurants, bars, cafes, and retail shops. Offered for sale in conjunction with 1410 30th Avenue, San Francisco, a 5-unit building in the Outer Sunset District. Please note: gross income includes Section-8 rent increases on 4 units effective July 1, 2025; pending approval by the SF Housing Authority."
